# schema-install-fallback walks up from its own directory for scripts/install.sh, copies the tracked files of core/, patterns/,
# templates/ and the two install scripts ONCE into a scratch work tree, and runs every install from that copy into an empty
# target; the repo's VERSION is not copied (arm VS writes a fake VERSION into the copy and commits it before the re-install). The five scripts under test are the ones that
# install lays down at scripts/ai-dlc/, taken from core/scripts/. A fixture's own directory is copied by the runner, never declared.
!scripts/install.sh
# install.sh sources its function file before it writes anything and refuses the install when it is absent.
scripts/install-scaffold-ignore.sh
# reason: core/ is enumerated -- the copy takes every tracked file under it except core/fixtures/ (named from the index, stubbed empty), and the copied install.sh globs core/scripts/*, core/hooks/*.sh, core/schemas/*.json and more; run.sh walks the installed scripts.
core/
patterns/
templates/
core/fixtures/lib/report.sh
core/fixtures/lib/world.sh
